Implemented the entire R2 shared owning scope against the accepted current scene source.

Request-local begin/commit/rollback/abort operations retain the outer draft and prefix identity/usability, guard every prefix finalizer and pre-request child, preserve bounded child-draft context, and clean up after cancellation. They restore suffix tables, image-pixel admission, diagnostics and publications, reclaim removed child/nested storage, and honestly retain spare capacity/history. No prefix/source snapshot or self-reference is used.

Typed active-draft source/group/shape owners support real empty-group filter planning/publication and later child ranges. Required production resolver/planner/media/session seams preserve explicit legacy fixtures without a default backend or implicit owned-stop conversion. The actual cached resolve/publication operation uses cache-borrowed stops and accepted opaque witnesses; 40000 fill/stroke instances share cache and scene stop allocations.

Computed pattern mapping survives suspension into actual PatternId fill/stroke publication and shape attachment. Same-job/source/generation output moves internally without pixel copying or a public raw buffer escape. Tickets validate sealed children, dimensions and scope; stale/canceled/error completions reclaim owning resources and suffix publications.

Public opaque ledger identity and LedgerBuffer operations use the accepted allocator for requested preallocation, actual-capacity admission, old/new overlap and controlled copy. Tests distinguish arithmetic overflow, native CapacityOverflow, retained registry metadata and physical-success history after cancellation, and enforce query's exact 65536 active-record limit including replacements. Clients explicitly release buffers; abandoned reservations remain conservative until ledger teardown. Existing scene/job budgets remain distinct.

All required offline commands passed: scene check, scene tests (**135 entries: unchanged111 + new24**), and frozen R2 validation. Every source/test is under800 lines; the only new test is744 lines. Audit:2853 protected files and1651 overlay protected paths, zero mismatches/new protected paths. Frozen HEAD and logical index remain unchanged; no index-writing commands ran (terminal index hash recorded; no before-byte hash was supplied).

README and APIcoverage.md provide integration/ownership examples; verification.json records exact logs and preservation. No missing protected-peer contract was found. Independent root review, fresh main checks and peer seeding remain coordinator gates after this terminal worker result. Full lower engines/adapters and product/oracle acceptance are separate scopes.

